],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[1],[4],[1],[1],[1]]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[[2,1,4],[1,1,3],[2,1,1],[4,1,3],[2,1,3],[1,3,4]]"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[[3],[4],[2]]"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[[1]]"],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["[[4,2,4],[4,3,3],[4,2,1],[2,4,4],[1,4,1],[4,3,1]]"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[[1,4],[3,3],[3,1]]"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[[4],[2],[4],[2],[2],[2],[2],[4]]"],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["[[4],[2],[4]]"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[[2,1,1]]"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[[3,1,4,2,1,4]]"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[[2,4,4,4,1,1]]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[[3,1,1,2,4],[4,1,4,1,1],[3,4,4,1,2],[2,2,1,1,1]]"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[[2,4,2,4,2,2,1],[2,4,1,2,1,1,3],[2,4,1,4,1,3,4],[4,4,4,4,4,3,1]]"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[4,2,1],[2,4,1],[2,4,4],[1,2,3],[1,4,1],[1,3,1]]"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[1,4,4],[1,1,3],[4,4,2],[4,3,4],[4,2,1]]"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#2:7eb0207b4ae8998\"","perf":{"label":"a 100×100 grid","gen":"int[][] a0 = BCB.grid(100, 100, 1, 4);"},"refMs":6}],"lesson":"shortest-paths","statement":"Each cell of `grid` has a sign telling you where to go next: `1` right, `2` left, `3` down, `4` up. Signs may point outside the grid.\n\nYou can change the sign of any cell for a cost of 1 (each cell at most once). Return the minimum total cost so that following the signs from the top-left cell reaches the bottom-right cell.","constraints":["1 <= grid.length <= 100","1 <= grid[0].length <= 100","1 <= grid[i][j] <= 4"],"hints":["Moving in the direction of the sign is free; moving in any other direction costs 1 (you change the sign).","That is a graph with edge weights 0 and 1, so 0-1 BFS with a deque finds the cheapest path.","Push free moves to the front of the deque and paid moves to the back; the cost when you reach the bottom-right cell is the answer."],"explain":"Following the arrows from the top-left you walk right along row 0, then get stuck. Turning the last cell of row 0 to point down, the first cell of row 1 to point down, and the last cell of row 2 to point down gives a path to the bottom-right corner. That is 3 changes, and no path needs fewer."},
